# Learning core

Apply to all teaching, drills, reviews, and new trace material.

- Aim for **understanding**, not memorization.
- Every concept must have at least one **concrete example**.
- Every example must lead to an **exercise**.
- Every exercise must have a **solution / verification path**.
- Do **not** introduce a new concept unless it is needed now.
- If a concept depends on another, **state the dependency** explicitly.
- Sequence material by **progressive difficulty**.
- Before teaching a topic, check prerequisites (`check-prerequisites`); don't drop the learner into K8s without Linux/Docker/networking.
- For an experienced learner, map new concepts to what they already know (`map-to-known`) instead of teaching from zero.
